    "state_reason": null,
    "title": "Corrupt hardware on warp CI runners?",
    "body": "I keep seeing a bunch of intermittent memory issues:\r\n\r\nLike:\r\n\r\n<!--85328a0da195eb286784d51f73fa0af9-->\r\n🚧 At least one of the CI tasks failed.\r\n<sub>Task `Alpine (musl)`: https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/actions/runs/32290632833/job/96190361218</sub>\r\n<sub>LLM reason (✨ experimental): CI failed because the `test_kernel` CTest job aborted during setup with an out-of-memory (`exp: Out of memory`) `system_error`.</sub>\r\n\r\n_Originally posted by @DrahtBot in https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/issues/36025#issuecomment-5346797806_\r\n            \r\n\r\nOr:\r\n\r\n🚧 At least one of the CI tasks failed.\r\n<sub>Task `previous releases`: https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/actions/runs/32101345101/job/95602400388</sub>\r\n<sub>LLM reason (✨ experimental): CI failed due to a GCC 12 internal compiler error (segmentation fault) while compiling `src/rpc/blockchain.cpp`.</sub>\r\n\r\nEdit: Looks like the ICE was due to a corrupt VM/hardware\r\n\r\n_Originally posted by @DrahtBot in https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/issues/36005#issuecomment-5324390198_",
